          "autoAdvance": false,
          "changeMeaning": "Opening title clip establishing the topic; nothing moves yet so students focus on the narration and the crowded, unarranged electron domains.",
          "narration": "Every covalent molecule has a three-dimensional shape, and that shape is not random. VSEPR theory \u2014 Valence Shell Electron Pair Repulsion \u2014 gives us a simple, powerful rule for predicting it. We begin with a central atom surrounded by regions of electron density we call electron domains."
        },
