                    120,
                    255
                  ],
                  "fontSize": 38
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "changeMeaning": "The title label updates to introduce the steric number concept, reinforcing counting of bonding and lone pairs as domains around the central atom.",
          "narration": "The total number of electron domains around the central atom is called the steric number. To find it, count the bonding pairs plus the lone pairs directly from a Lewis structure. Here we have four domains, so the steric number is four \u2014 and that number alone determines the underlying geometry."
        }
      ]
